<article class="env-exercise" id="03VL">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03VL">Exercise <span data-tag="03VL">8.4.1.12</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{Cat}$ denote the (ordinary) category of small categories, and let $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\leq 1} \subset \operatorname{Cat}$ denote the full subcategory spanned by the objects $[0]$ and $[1]$. Show that: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The full subcategory $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\leq 1}$ generates $\operatorname{Cat}$ under colimits. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A small category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ can be realized as the colimit (in $\operatorname{Cat}$) of a diagram $\mathcal{K} \rightarrow \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\leq 1}$ if and only if the category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is free, in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="00HR" href="/tag/00HR">1.3.7.7</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> In particular, the inclusion $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\leq 1} ) \subset \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Cat})$ satisfies condition $(3)$ of Warning <a data-tag="03VJ" href="/tag/03VJ">8.4.1.10</a>, but does not satisfy condition $(2)$. </p>
</article>
